When a clearing <br> ends the last line of a block container, Ladybird
makes that line reach down to the clearance, so the block ends below the
floats it clears — however much room the floats left beside the break.

Gecko, Blink and WebKit all do the same. Gecko’s nsBlockFrame::
ReflowDirtyLines() clears the floats after the block’s last
line (“BR-clearance from the last line of the block”). Blink’s
InlineLayoutAlgorithm::AddAnyClearanceAfterLine() records the exclusion
space’s clearance offset with SetClearanceAfterLine(). And WebKit’s
InlineFormattingContext::updateLayoutStateWithLineLayoutResult() sets
the gap after the last line from logicalTopForNextLine(), which takes
the break’s clear into account.
